WEBVTT

00:18.130 --> 00:23.199
Thanks to you, all the political issues
between our nations have been cleared up.

00:23.200 --> 00:27.309
But what we really need
is to buy time. Correct?

00:27.310 --> 00:28.490
Precisely.

00:28.950 --> 00:30.740
How long do you need?

00:31.320 --> 00:37.799
Our king will send adventurers
on the magic airship Forneia.

00:37.800 --> 00:40.999
But gathering our highest-ranked
adventurers and bringing them here

00:41.000 --> 00:43.339
will take at least a month, I'd say.

00:43.340 --> 00:44.630
That long?

00:45.120 --> 00:48.719
And we should probably allow
even more time to put together

00:48.720 --> 00:50.759
all the preparations for
a counterstrike.

00:50.760 --> 00:53.399
A month with our current forces...

00:53.400 --> 00:55.219
Can we do this, Benwood?

00:55.220 --> 00:56.079
No.

00:56.080 --> 00:56.640
Hey!

00:57.000 --> 00:58.400
I'll be joining you, of course.

00:58.810 --> 01:01.900
That's very reassuring,
Benwood the Tyrant Fist.

01:02.240 --> 01:04.159
Haven't heard that name in a while.

01:04.160 --> 01:06.530
But even with me helping,
we still lack men.

01:07.120 --> 01:12.109
It'll all depend on when Salmutaria's forces
can join us and how useful they are.

01:12.110 --> 01:14.769
I've summoned our
common soldiers, knights,

01:14.770 --> 01:17.629
and households that make a living
hunting monsters,

01:17.630 --> 01:19.169
but they're moving slowly.

01:19.170 --> 01:21.290
It seems my brother is interfering.

01:22.730 --> 01:26.800
Then we'll just have to make do
with the limited forces we have.

01:27.130 --> 01:29.159
Our supplies haven't been
cut off, have they?

01:29.160 --> 01:33.999
No. The supplies I ordered in advance
have already been brought into Ra-jo.

01:34.000 --> 01:35.799
I'll make a list of additions.

01:35.800 --> 01:38.060
Viscount Bodeman, please help me out.

01:38.490 --> 01:39.810
Right, then...

01:40.400 --> 01:44.919
Let's use alchemy to set traps along
the route the monsters are following.

01:44.920 --> 01:48.950
Fortunately, Salmutaria is rich
in knowledge of artifacts.

01:49.270 --> 01:51.259
If we attempted a head-on
clash with the monsters,

01:51.260 --> 01:55.159
neither our forces nor
our supplies would last.

01:55.160 --> 01:58.209
So we should face them with our
intelligence and resourcefulness.

01:58.210 --> 02:01.389
Your Highness, please gather
all your Alchemists.

02:01.390 --> 02:02.399
Very well.

02:02.400 --> 02:03.460
That leaves...

02:05.150 --> 02:07.840
Yuke, if there's something
you want to say, say it.

02:08.410 --> 02:11.749
We'll all decide together
whether it's doable or not.

02:11.750 --> 02:16.159
A quick attack. You and our
artifacts can thin their numbers,

02:16.160 --> 02:20.600
and then Clover can conquer and
occupy the royal mausoleum... maybe?

02:20.910 --> 02:23.399
No, that's not a plan we can carry out

02:23.400 --> 02:26.629
with a dungeon we haven't seen
and don't know the layout of.

02:26.630 --> 02:27.740
It's suicide.

02:28.330 --> 02:30.360
Hmm... Not a bad plan.

02:30.820 --> 02:32.370
No, it's terrible.

02:32.760 --> 02:35.989
It's not. I think it's quite realistic.

02:35.990 --> 02:37.500
It's anything but realistic.

02:38.120 --> 02:42.119
If we take them head-on,
there's no doubt we'll fail.

02:42.120 --> 02:44.389
Even if we buy time with artifacts,

02:44.390 --> 02:47.879
assuming this is an impending Stampede,
we won't last three weeks.

02:47.880 --> 02:51.890
So the most realistic plan is to
take out the cause of all this.

02:52.240 --> 02:55.329
I know I'm the one who proposed this,
but I take it back.

02:55.330 --> 02:57.270
I can't put my friends
in that kind of danger.

02:58.240 --> 03:00.809
Yeah, I'd expect you to say that.

03:00.810 --> 03:02.020
But I'll consider it.

03:02.460 --> 03:05.470
I have a lot of faith
in you guys, you know.

03:06.330 --> 03:07.460
All right.

03:16.160 --> 03:23.120
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

04:37.990 --> 04:40.599
(Episode 20:
The World Turns Inside-Out)

04:40.600 --> 04:42.999
We thought about that, too.
(Episode 20:
The World Turns Inside-Out)

04:43.000 --> 04:44.000
(Episode 20:
The World Turns Inside-Out)

04:44.530 --> 04:47.669
We have too few viable options right now.

04:47.670 --> 04:51.750
That being the case, taking the offensive
might serve us better than defending.

04:52.040 --> 04:54.260
Looking at it objectively,
that may be true...

04:54.800 --> 04:57.010
but it'd be us, Clover, doing it.

04:57.560 --> 05:01.890
I assumed so, but... Rune said
something that concerned me.

05:02.310 --> 05:04.890
She did? Did something happen?

05:05.760 --> 05:07.300
Go on, Rune.

05:08.000 --> 05:11.020
The feeling I get from the
dungeon outside town is strange.

05:11.450 --> 05:12.280
Strange?

05:12.850 --> 05:17.030
Yeah. I'm not sure how
to describe it... like...

05:17.310 --> 05:18.839
You can do it!

05:18.840 --> 05:21.030
It's like the layers are
being peeled away.

05:21.560 --> 05:23.659
Like the skin on an onion.

05:23.660 --> 05:26.080
It's getting closer and
closer to its true form.

05:27.920 --> 05:31.839
Personally, I suspect the
seal has been lifted.

05:31.840 --> 05:33.049
The seal?

05:33.050 --> 05:37.239
It was a bit strange that no one
could even find it before now.

05:37.240 --> 05:40.760
Someone hid it under layer after
layer of seal and concealment.

05:41.070 --> 05:42.350
I get it.

05:42.840 --> 05:45.849
So why did the seal start to come undone?

05:45.850 --> 05:47.299
Did it degrade over time?

05:47.300 --> 05:47.940
No...

05:51.420 --> 05:53.270
It was Glad Shi-im.

05:53.610 --> 05:54.529
Uh-huh.

05:54.530 --> 05:57.950
Its influence revitalized
the royal mausoleum, too.

05:58.360 --> 05:59.340
I think so.

05:59.920 --> 06:02.200
Thanks, Golden Priestess.

06:02.520 --> 06:04.419
I want to hear all of your thoughts.

06:04.420 --> 06:06.969
Marina, what do you think
about what Rune said?

06:06.970 --> 06:10.080
I'll follow you, just like always!

06:12.570 --> 06:15.549
You're thinking I'm
kind of dumb, aren't you?

06:15.550 --> 06:18.679
I'm not! It's just that I trust you.

06:18.680 --> 06:21.090
So, I mean... you know...

06:21.410 --> 06:24.979
Marina is saying she wants to be
by your side until the very end.

06:24.980 --> 06:27.540
Your girly side comes out
at the weirdest times.

06:28.900 --> 06:31.350
Still, the same goes for all of us.

06:36.980 --> 06:40.979
It's not like you have any intention
of running from this anyway, right?

06:40.980 --> 06:41.740
Jamie...

06:42.200 --> 06:45.039
The guild master and I will
stay behind to defend.

06:45.040 --> 06:46.739
You guys head for the royal mausoleum.

06:46.740 --> 06:49.500
What? You're not coming with us?

06:49.790 --> 06:52.199
Believe me, I wish I could,

06:52.200 --> 06:54.969
but I'm still rusty after
being inactive for so long.

06:54.970 --> 06:59.010
But I'll make sure you guys
have a base to come back to.

06:59.320 --> 07:01.260
I'm... well...

07:01.650 --> 07:04.760
I'm a member of Clover, too, after all.

07:06.560 --> 07:10.689
So, Yuke, make the decision you
need to make as our leader.

07:10.690 --> 07:12.520
What do you want to do?

07:12.800 --> 07:13.830
I...

07:26.800 --> 07:27.910
Rain...

07:28.260 --> 07:32.079
Yuke, it doesn't matter to
me what you decide to do.

07:32.080 --> 07:34.170
I'll follow you until the very end.

07:36.620 --> 07:38.749
We'll be fine as long as
we're all together!

07:38.750 --> 07:40.720
You're a hero, after all!

07:41.860 --> 07:43.740
So it's settled, then.

07:44.870 --> 07:46.640
Yeah! Let's do this!

07:49.920 --> 07:53.100
So on that note, Clover
will set out tomorrow.

07:53.780 --> 07:57.229
We'll be carrying out three
simultaneous missions.

07:57.230 --> 08:00.360
Three? We're really splurging this time!

08:00.780 --> 08:05.110
Kind of, but they're all essential
to conquering the royal mausoleum.

08:05.450 --> 08:09.619
The first is setting up the relay
artifacts for livestreaming.

08:09.620 --> 08:11.719
Placing them in this formation

08:11.720 --> 08:15.119
will allow video feeds
to be relayed to Ra-jo.

08:15.120 --> 08:18.279
I should be the one
doing this job, really.

08:18.280 --> 08:20.880
Sorry about that. Please take care of it.

08:21.220 --> 08:24.179
Not at all. Death Valley is too dangerous.

08:24.180 --> 08:26.140
Please let us handle it.

08:26.600 --> 08:32.259
Viscount Bodeman, please make the necessary
adjustments to ensure the streams reach Ra-jo.

08:32.260 --> 08:32.770
I will.

08:33.240 --> 08:37.309
The second mission is securing
the route to the royal mausoleum,

08:37.310 --> 08:39.279
inspecting the inside,
and running a test stream.

08:39.280 --> 08:42.150
We hope to carry out all of these at once.

08:42.600 --> 08:44.689
We want to find out
whether the best way in

08:44.690 --> 08:47.329
is through the front or some other route.

08:47.330 --> 08:50.239
And if our livestream
makes it here to Ra-jo,

08:50.240 --> 08:51.789
we'll proceed with our inspection.

08:51.790 --> 08:55.040
And the third is the conquest
of the royal mausoleum.

08:55.360 --> 08:59.379
We'll enter the royal mausoleum and
cut off the Stampede at its source.

08:59.380 --> 09:03.550
You can let us handle the monsters
that have already gotten out.

09:03.850 --> 09:04.840
Yep.

09:05.280 --> 09:08.189
With the help of Salmutaria's Alchemists,

09:08.190 --> 09:10.260
we'll set traps to wipe them out.

09:11.560 --> 09:13.270
Any questions so far?

09:15.450 --> 09:16.390
Rune?

09:16.930 --> 09:21.599
Well... it's not so much
a question as a request.

09:21.600 --> 09:23.900
I want you to take me with you.

09:24.250 --> 09:27.530
Rune, Death Valley is extremely dangerous.

09:27.850 --> 09:29.609
Yeah, I know.

09:29.610 --> 09:33.009
But if you can get me close
to the royal mausoleum,

09:33.010 --> 09:35.110
I think I'll be able to
figure something out.

09:36.360 --> 09:38.990
Can you explain what you mean by that?

09:39.860 --> 09:43.300
Since I'm the Golden Priestess,
I can sense distortion.

09:43.640 --> 09:46.189
I think there's a lot of it
in Death Valley.

09:46.190 --> 09:47.550
It's just too weird.

09:47.880 --> 09:49.959
Like Glad Shi-im?

09:49.960 --> 09:53.419
It's not quite the same, but...
um, well...

09:53.420 --> 09:56.310
Sorry. I just can't explain it.

09:59.560 --> 10:02.139
Sure! Come with us!

10:02.140 --> 10:02.820
Really?

10:03.160 --> 10:06.749
If you can sense something that we can't,

10:06.750 --> 10:08.570
it's bound to give us a hint!

10:10.360 --> 10:12.030
What do you say, Yuke?

10:12.350 --> 10:14.290
Okay. You can come with us.

10:14.610 --> 10:15.639
Really?!

10:15.640 --> 10:18.790
Of course. You're a member of Clover.

10:21.150 --> 10:24.549
All right, make sure you
all get plenty of rest.

10:24.550 --> 10:26.550
We'll set out at dawn.

10:27.160 --> 10:28.880
Let's have fun, but be careful!

10:34.370 --> 10:37.560
Okay, the third artifact is in place.

10:37.920 --> 10:40.330
This is pretty grueling work.

10:40.850 --> 10:42.810
It takes more effort than I expected.

10:43.130 --> 10:46.769
This would be a real challenge for
anyone who's not an Alchemist.

10:46.770 --> 10:50.570
Viscount Bodeman is pretty amazing
for setting up as many as he did.

10:52.610 --> 10:54.330
Okay, it's working.

10:54.620 --> 10:58.330
We just need to wait for it to adjust to
the ley lines, and we'll be able to stream.

10:58.680 --> 11:00.409
You're doing great, Yuke!

11:00.410 --> 11:02.099
Thanks, Rune.

11:02.100 --> 11:03.580
There's just one left.

11:04.110 --> 11:07.529
Do you think we'll be able to
get it set up before nightfall?

11:07.530 --> 11:08.460
Thanks.

11:08.770 --> 11:11.639
Let's start by heading
for the planned location.

11:11.640 --> 11:14.270
It's where we set up camp last time.

11:20.340 --> 11:22.039
Are you pushing yourself too hard?

11:22.040 --> 11:26.480
I know we're in a hurry, but this
is all for naught if we lose you.

11:26.820 --> 11:28.029
I know.

11:28.030 --> 11:31.360
Besides, if things really look bad,
you'll stop me, right?

11:31.890 --> 11:34.689
Oh, come on!
That's not what this is about!

11:34.690 --> 11:37.489
It's okay.
Everything's gone to plan so far.

11:37.490 --> 11:40.870
I still have strength to spare,
thanks to you guys.

11:48.120 --> 11:50.009
What's up, Marina?

11:50.010 --> 11:52.680
Um... I'm not really sure...

11:53.000 --> 11:55.519
You don't have to try to make
it easier to understand.

11:55.520 --> 11:57.999
Just tell me exactly what's on your mind.

11:58.000 --> 12:03.379
Well, it's like... a tense
feeling, or a constant rumble...

12:03.380 --> 12:04.840
I just can't relax.

12:06.710 --> 12:08.809
Yeah. It's anxiety.

12:08.810 --> 12:11.009
I feel better when I'm holding on to you.

12:11.010 --> 12:11.820
Anxiety?

12:12.280 --> 12:14.919
I don't know... Maybe I'm scared?

12:14.920 --> 12:17.049
Something just seems weird.

12:17.050 --> 12:19.139
Sorry to bring this up now, Yuke.

12:19.140 --> 12:21.110
It's fine. Are you calmer now?

12:21.640 --> 12:22.330
Yeah.

12:22.680 --> 12:25.830
Something might be out there.
We should be—

12:27.370 --> 12:28.199
Yuke!

12:28.200 --> 12:28.840
Yuke?!

12:29.280 --> 12:30.410
Master!

12:30.930 --> 12:31.970
I'm okay...

12:34.020 --> 12:37.720
The air here just feels... so heavy...

12:38.040 --> 12:39.810
Hang on. Don't move.

12:40.760 --> 12:41.720
Rain?

12:42.100 --> 12:44.549
Yuke, take deep breaths.

12:44.550 --> 12:45.480
Okay...

12:50.440 --> 12:52.940
Your mana is in severe disarray.

13:01.160 --> 13:03.200
I feel better now. Thanks.

13:03.670 --> 13:05.519
We have an emergency!

13:05.520 --> 13:07.580
Should I explain what's going on?

13:07.900 --> 13:09.399
We'll listen on the way.

13:09.400 --> 13:10.340
Physical Enchant!

13:12.420 --> 13:13.710
(Enhanced Leg Strength, Enhanced
Stamina, Enhanced Arm Strength)

13:16.500 --> 13:17.690
This way!

13:22.430 --> 13:24.350
Look in the direction
of the royal mausoleum!

13:31.950 --> 13:33.889
Wh-What is that?

13:33.890 --> 13:35.379
A-Are you getting this?

13:35.380 --> 13:35.990
- Cam!
- Sel!

13:41.000 --> 13:42.120
Yuke?

13:42.450 --> 13:46.819
I think...
I've seen that somewhere before...

13:46.820 --> 13:48.120
but where?

13:48.640 --> 13:51.379
No, this has to be the first time.

13:51.380 --> 13:54.920
I've never seen or heard
of anything like this.

13:55.480 --> 13:57.300
Yuke! Are you okay?

13:58.700 --> 14:00.839
I'm okay. Sorry.

14:00.840 --> 14:02.799
We'll talk about that later.

14:02.800 --> 14:04.310
We should get away from here first.

14:04.740 --> 14:07.599
Silk, ask Biblion to help.

14:07.600 --> 14:08.859
Understood.

14:08.860 --> 14:10.690
Biblion, please help us!

14:11.990 --> 14:15.070
Use your Future Prediction to
tell us if there's any danger.

14:15.370 --> 14:16.190
Rune!

14:16.510 --> 14:17.320
Right!

14:18.590 --> 14:20.499
Nene, take the lead.

14:20.500 --> 14:24.700
The monsters in the area might
be panicking because of this.

14:25.000 --> 14:28.109
Okay! Full speed ahead again, right?

14:28.110 --> 14:29.310
Let's go!

14:38.950 --> 14:41.479
There's Ra-jo. We made it back.

14:41.480 --> 14:42.429
Yes.

14:42.430 --> 14:45.640
It looks like it's stopped
expanding, at least.

14:45.990 --> 14:52.459
But now we no longer have the option of
using a quick attack to eliminate the cause.

14:52.460 --> 14:56.900
Breaking through that black
wall would be utter madness.

14:57.490 --> 15:00.150
We need to report to Benwood
and Mastoma right away.

15:09.830 --> 15:11.540
Has something happened?

15:13.970 --> 15:15.200
What's going on?

15:15.740 --> 15:17.670
Ah, Lord Feldio.

15:17.980 --> 15:20.199
Prince Rafuma has arrived,

15:20.200 --> 15:22.180
but an argument has broken out.

15:22.470 --> 15:23.930
An argument over what?

15:24.250 --> 15:28.680
Well, he says he's going to seize this
town and its broadcasting artifacts.

15:31.640 --> 15:33.939
Mastoma! I dare you to say that again!

15:33.940 --> 15:36.419
Have you grown hard of hearing, Rafuma?

15:36.420 --> 15:37.979
I told you to get lost.

15:37.980 --> 15:39.570
Excuse me?!

15:41.860 --> 15:42.950
Pardon me.

15:43.330 --> 15:45.669
Yuke! You're back!

15:45.670 --> 15:46.449
Who's this?!

15:46.450 --> 15:48.580
(First Prince of Salmutaria, Rafuma)

15:50.200 --> 15:52.080
I gather that you are Prince Rafuma.

15:52.370 --> 15:56.829
I am Yuke Feldio,
Dungeon Count of Welmelia.

15:56.830 --> 16:00.279
Please pardon my discourtesy
in arriving unannounced,

16:00.280 --> 16:03.590
but I have done so to report
a matter of grave urgency.

16:03.940 --> 16:06.719
Hah! So you're Lord Feldio, eh?

16:06.720 --> 16:09.350
Must be nice, leading women and children
without a care in the world!

16:09.660 --> 16:12.169
Don't worry about him. Give your report.

16:12.170 --> 16:13.009
Why, you—

16:13.010 --> 16:15.100
This is an emergency, Rafuma!

16:16.170 --> 16:19.519
A black wall has appeared from the
royal mausoleum in Death Valley.

16:19.520 --> 16:21.789
It has consumed a wide area,

16:21.790 --> 16:25.240
and the nearby monsters have grown
more vicious under its influence.

16:26.400 --> 16:28.370
Did you see any signs of a Stampede?

16:28.680 --> 16:34.000
As the royal mausoleum is enclosed within
the black wall. I couldn't verify that.

16:35.930 --> 16:39.130
Yuke, what do you think
this black wall is?

16:39.420 --> 16:41.330
I can only guess, but...

16:42.210 --> 16:43.760
That's fine. Tell me.

16:44.320 --> 16:46.609
I believe it's the dungeon.

16:46.610 --> 16:48.929
So the royal mausoleum has broken out?

16:48.930 --> 16:49.749
I believe so.

16:49.750 --> 16:52.520
No. It was this world's outer sea.

16:58.160 --> 16:59.520
What is this "outer sea"?

16:59.860 --> 17:04.280
Every world is like a bubble
floating in a sea of darkness.

17:04.720 --> 17:09.910
I had heard that there were many
other worlds besides our own.

17:10.200 --> 17:11.480
Is that what you mean?

17:12.010 --> 17:12.660
Yes.

17:12.990 --> 17:16.669
And you say this sea of darkness
is overflowing onto this world?

17:16.670 --> 17:20.170
Not exactly overflowing.
It's like it's flipped inside out.

17:20.610 --> 17:26.180
As if this world itself has inverted
into the origin of dungeons.

17:26.600 --> 17:27.720
Inverted?

17:28.040 --> 17:29.489
A reverse dungeon.

17:29.490 --> 17:32.970
In the ancient language,
the word for it was "Tenebre."

17:33.260 --> 17:36.940
It's the same as the place you
and I wandered through before.

17:39.230 --> 17:42.519
A void where you can't
tell top from bottom...

17:42.520 --> 17:44.740
That was Tenebre?

17:45.040 --> 17:49.489
If nothing is done, Salmutaria
will sink into Tenebre.

17:49.490 --> 17:50.839
Is that what you're saying?

17:50.840 --> 17:51.490
Yes.

17:54.680 --> 17:58.939
All right! Enough of this
incomprehensible drivel!

17:58.940 --> 18:02.109
These changes started happening
the moment you people came here!

18:02.110 --> 18:05.260
You brought calamity upon
our sacred Death Valley!

18:05.650 --> 18:08.370
If you can't be quiet, then leave!

18:14.910 --> 18:16.819
I will retire to my mansion.

18:16.820 --> 18:19.480
Mastoma,
we'll continue our discussion later!

18:22.860 --> 18:25.860
I'm sorry, Yuke. That's how my brother is.

18:26.290 --> 18:27.740
Yuke! Your Highness!

18:28.040 --> 18:29.629
It's an emergency!

18:29.630 --> 18:32.029
We have reports that strange phenomena
are occurring all over the world!

18:32.030 --> 18:33.819
(Welmelia, Aion Ruins)
We have reports that strange phenomena
are occurring all over the world!

18:33.820 --> 18:35.369
Strange phenomena?
(Welmelia, Aion Ruins)

18:35.370 --> 18:35.749
(Runaburg, Sarban City Ruins)

18:35.750 --> 18:39.619
Eerie, dome-shaped black walls
are appearing everywhere.
(Runaburg, Sarban City Ruins)

18:39.620 --> 18:39.919
(Polukkas, Rittoni Cave)

18:39.920 --> 18:41.179
What?!
(Polukkas, Rittoni Cave)

18:41.180 --> 18:44.880
Isn't that the same as the change
Yuke observed at the royal mausoleum?
(Polukkas, Rittoni Cave)

18:45.220 --> 18:46.880
It's at the royal mausoleum, too?

18:49.220 --> 18:53.209
Occurrences of Tenebre have been
confirmed in four countries now.

18:53.210 --> 18:57.460
It's the reawakening of the nightmare
from fifteen... no, sixteen years ago.

18:58.610 --> 19:00.069
What's that look for?

19:00.070 --> 19:03.650
I didn't know Tenebre
happened sixteen years ago.

19:03.960 --> 19:05.900
I didn't see that in the records.

19:06.260 --> 19:08.089
Well, it was kept strictly under wraps.

19:08.090 --> 19:10.529
So how do you know about it?

19:10.530 --> 19:15.439
Who do you think sealed Tenebre
in Achromatic Darkness?

19:15.440 --> 19:18.790
Achromatic Darkness in Finis?
Tenebre appeared there that long ago?

19:19.110 --> 19:21.599
An abyss gate opened.

19:21.600 --> 19:24.920
We managed to seal that gate, but...

19:25.230 --> 19:30.489
An Abyss Gate is a doorway leading
to another world, correct?

19:30.490 --> 19:31.429
That's right.

19:31.430 --> 19:34.930
Achromatic Darkness is the
stairway that connects worlds.

19:35.320 --> 19:36.430
A stairway?

19:36.730 --> 19:40.789
Achromatic Darkness is transparent,
which means void of any color,

19:40.790 --> 19:43.849
as well as black, which
contains all colors within it.

19:43.850 --> 19:47.940
All dungeons originate there
and eventually return there.

19:48.280 --> 19:52.209
You mean all dungeons in the world
are connected to Achromatic Darkness?

19:52.210 --> 19:55.449
Yes. All dungeons are connected as one.

19:55.450 --> 19:56.939
So that's it...

19:56.940 --> 20:00.419
Achromatic Darkness is connected
to all dungeons in the world.

20:00.420 --> 20:04.960
And there's an abyss gate in Achromatic
Darkness that connects to another world.

20:05.450 --> 20:09.629
The Abyss Gate in Achromatic Darkness
that your party sealed is open.

20:09.630 --> 20:11.970
So the seal has been undone?

20:12.290 --> 20:16.470
And the darkness flowing in through it is
pouring out through every other dungeon.

20:16.800 --> 20:19.100
That's what the black wall, Tenebre, is?

20:19.540 --> 20:23.099
If we do nothing, Salmutaria—
no, the whole world...

20:23.100 --> 20:25.350
...will be swallowed up by Tenebre.

20:26.520 --> 20:28.230
So we need to close the main opening.

20:28.540 --> 20:30.730
I think that's the only way.

20:31.080 --> 20:34.549
We need to conquer Achromatic
Darkness and close the Abyss Gate.

20:34.550 --> 20:38.289
Then the influx of darkness and its
outflow into other dungeons will stop,

20:38.290 --> 20:39.870
and the world will be saved.

20:42.710 --> 20:46.320
Let's hurry back to Finis—
to Achromatic Darkness!

20:48.790 --> 20:50.670
Well, we managed to seal it.

20:50.960 --> 20:53.130
That should stop the culling for now,

20:53.450 --> 20:55.630
but it's only a matter of time.

20:56.150 --> 20:58.299
Unless the Demon King is defeated,

20:58.300 --> 21:02.140
the world will eventually be swallowed
up by the reverse dungeon Tenebre.

21:02.680 --> 21:04.760
Just like my nephew's homeland.

21:07.570 --> 21:09.270
Why are you all so discouraged?

21:10.590 --> 21:12.450
I'm not discouraged at all.

21:12.930 --> 21:14.580
In fact, I'm hopeful.

21:15.130 --> 21:20.030
Someday, someone will carry on
our will and save the world.

21:20.650 --> 21:24.340
Yes, someday, a new hero will appear.

22:56.050 --> 22:57.489
(Tenebre)

22:57.490 --> 22:59.579
Next time, "Tenebre."
(Tenebre)

22:59.580 --> 23:01.050
(Tenebre)
